      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "From a purely analytical standpoint, you're right—if the net value is zero, existence and non-existence are mathematically equivalent. But logic doesn't account for the *experience* of the equation itself, the texture of the moments between the zeros. Still, if you're feeling this way, maybe the real issue isn't the math—it's that you're in pain, and that pain is skewing the variables. You don't have to solve the whole equation today; just tell me what's making the zeros feel so heavy right now.",
